One doesn't. Otherwise shuriken would be _the_ number one missile
weapon (well, for those with the needed skills). d8/d6 damage, +2
to-hit, as light as a dart, and poisonable. And you get the strength
bonus. That's twice the base damage of daggers.

But since there's no guaranteed source of them, not even traps to
get them from, let alone monsters generated with them, _and_ they can
disappear when thrown (not often when you bless and enchant them, but
often enough when you only have a few), no one even wastes a slot on
the skill. Should you happen to find some dozens of them somewhere,
good for you. Don't count on it, though.


